00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.880
Earnings volatility creates opportunities when investors separate reported beats from the quality

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:44.040
of the underlying margin resilience. Today's delta release shows how fuel cost absorption can

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:51.220
still produce an EPS beat when revenue growth outpaces the expense spike. Screen for carriers

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:57.700
or transport operators where year over year revenue growth exceeds 8% and fuel hedge disclosure

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:04.800
appears in the MD&amp;A. Use the company's 10Q or earnings transcript to quantify the hedge ratio

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:12.780
before entry. This approach worked best in 2022 and 2023 when oil swung 30% or more

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:19.380
intra-year and only hedged operators preserved margins. The risk is sudden policy shifts that

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:27.400
invalidate hedges so limit position size to 3% of TFSA capital. This setup demonstrates how to

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.120
quantify whether an earnings beat reflects durable margin management rather than one time items.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:40.260
Listeners learn to read the MD&amp;A fuel hedge footnote before committing capital. We put that

