00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:57.500
pattern and adjusting screens accordingly. Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:04.620
and it cost me money before I figured it out. Imagine you added 3% bitcoin exposure via the

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:15.240
Canadian listed BTCXETF to your TFSA last quarter when the S&amp;P 500 dipped 4%. Your order filled at

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:22.400
the market opened but the actual mechanics between click and fill included a 0.8% premium to spot

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:32.580
plus the ETF's 0.45% management fee that compounds daily. Bitcoin's 0.15 correlation to the TSX

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:39.700
composite over the past 12 months improves the efficient frontier at 1-3% allocation. Yet that

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:46.320
correlation spiked above 0.6 during the March banking stress window, erasing the diversification

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:53.000
benefit exactly when it was needed. Professionals always cross check the ETF's premium or discount

00:08:53.000 --> 00:09:00.460
to NAV on the exchange before buying and set a hard 5% portfolio cap so volatility cannot overwhelm

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:06.260
the rest of the book. The biggest mistake with crypto allocation is treating the 1-5%

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:12.900
band as a starting point rather than a ceiling. Instead, size the position so a 50% drawdown in

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:20.320
the crypto sleeve produces no more than a 2.5% portfolio loss. Before we wrap, open your brokerage

